itle":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:c8e8fe4edfb6291480e8f4f3e24350e6b12c4ee78412831a11da9c91490e9f3e","file":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex","line":110,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"8af11a4c1904451eaf09d40c3709ad344a8dd9d5e5384a6322d036141a1e1c0d","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c8e8fe4edfb6291480e8f4f3e24350e6b12c4ee78412831a11da9c91490e9f3e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex#L110"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:stable-finiteness}\n\\leavevmode\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n\\item There are two unital simple stably finite complex \\(C^*\\)-algebras\nwhose minimal tensor product is properly infinite. One factor can be\ntaken to be \\(C_r^*(\\mathbb F_2)\\).\n\\item There is a separable unital complex \\(C^*\\)-algebra \\(B\\) admitting\na normalized \\(2\\)-quasitrace such that\n\\(B\\otimes_{\\min}C_r^*(\\mathbb F_2)\\) is properly infinite and admits no\nnormalized \\(2\\)-quasitrace.\n\\item There is a separable unital stably finite complex \\(C^*\\)-algebra\nwith no tracial state.\n\\end{enumerate}"}
